# Database Schema & Prisma

## Schema Overview
The database schema is defined in [prisma/schema.prisma](mdc:prisma/schema.prisma) and uses PostgreSQL with Prisma ORM.

## Core Tables

### Layouts
```prisma
model layouts {
  id            String   @id @default(cuid())
  name          String
  layout_image  String
  is_active     Boolean  @default(true)
  created_at    DateTime @default(now())
  updated_at    DateTime @updatedAt
}
```

### Layout Fields
```prisma
model layout_fields {
  id           String   @id @default(cuid())
  layout_id    String
  field_name   String
  field_type   String   // 'manual' or 'auto_calculated'
  is_visible   Boolean  @default(true)
  display_name String
  unit         String?  // 'inches', 'sqft', etc.
  layout       layouts  @relation(fields: [layout_id], references: [id])
}
```

### Materials
```prisma
model materials {
  id              String   @id @default(cuid())
  name            String
  brand           String
  price_per_sqft  Float
  is_active       Boolean  @default(true)
  created_at      DateTime @default(now())
  updated_at      DateTime @updatedAt
}
```

### Edge Styles
```prisma
model edge_styles {
  id                    String   @id @default(cuid())
  name                  String
  thickness             String
  price_per_linear_ft   Float
  is_active             Boolean  @default(true)
  created_at            DateTime @default(now())
  updated_at            DateTime @updatedAt
}
```

### Auto Calculation Rules
```prisma
model auto_calculation_rules {
  id           String   @id @default(cuid())
  layout_id    String
  rule_name    String
  formula      String
  is_active    Boolean  @default(true)
  layout       layouts  @relation(fields: [layout_id], references: [id])
}
```

### Layout Field Groups
```prisma
model layout_field_groups {
  id           String   @id @default(cuid())
  layout_id    String
  group_name   String
  display_name String
  is_active    Boolean  @default(true)
  layout       layouts  @relation(fields: [layout_id], references: [id])
}
```

### Leads
```prisma
model leads {
  id           String   @id @default(cuid())
  full_name    String
  email        String
  phone        String
  street_address String
  zip_code     String
  city         String
  state        String
  created_at   DateTime @default(now())
}
```

## API Routes
API routes are located in `app/api/` and follow RESTful patterns:

### Layouts API
- `GET /api/layouts` - Get all active layouts
- `GET /api/layout-fields/[layoutId]` - Get fields for specific layout
- `GET /api/auto-calculation-rules/[layoutId]` - Get calculation rules
- `GET /api/layout-field-groups/[layoutId]` - Get field groups

### Materials & Edges API
- `GET /api/materials` - Get all active materials
- `GET /api/edge-styles` - Get all active edge styles

## Prisma Client Usage
```typescript
// In API routes
import { prisma } from '@/lib/prisma';

// Get all active layouts
const layouts = await prisma.layouts.findMany({
  where: { is_active: true },
  orderBy: { name: 'asc' }
});

// Get layout fields with layout relation
const fields = await prisma.layout_fields.findMany({
  where: { 
    layout_id: layoutId,
    is_visible: true 
  },
  include: { layout: true }
});
```

## Database Relationships
- **One-to-Many**: Layout → Layout Fields, Auto Calculation Rules, Field Groups
- **Foreign Keys**: All related tables reference layouts.id
- **Soft Deletes**: Use is_active flag instead of hard deletes

## Data Validation
- **Required Fields**: Enforced at database level
- **Type Safety**: Prisma provides TypeScript types
- **Constraints**: Unique constraints where needed
- **Defaults**: Sensible defaults for common fields

## Performance Considerations
- **Indexes**: Primary keys and foreign keys are indexed
- **Selective Queries**: Only fetch needed fields
- **Relations**: Use include for related data
- **Pagination**: Implement for large datasets
